// Seeing the music
// While music plays, the steps that
// sound light up in the code. If they
// don't, turn on Highlight playing
// steps in Settings.
//
// Try: play and follow the lights.
// Edit while it plays: the lights
// follow your edits.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd [~ bd] sd ~, hh*8")
$: note("<c3 eb3> g3").s("piano")
// ---
// Piano roll
// ._pianoroll() draws the notes under
// the line that makes them: time goes
// left to right, pitch goes up.
//
// Try: change the notes and Update.

setcpm(30)
$: n("0 2 4 <6 7> 4 2")
  .scale("C:minor")
  .s("triangle")
  ._pianoroll()
// ---
// More pictures
// ._punchcard() draws each event as a
// block; ._scope() draws the sound
// wave itself.
//
// Try: move ._scope() to the drums.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd*2 sd, hh*8")._punchcard()
$: note("c2 c3").s("sawtooth")
  .lpf(800)._scope()
// ---
// Colors
// .color() sets the color of a
// layer's lights and pictures.
//
// Try: orange, cyan, magenta, lime.

setcpm(30)
$: s("bd*2 sd")
  .color("orange")._punchcard()
$: s("hh*8").gain(0.5)
  .color("cyan")._punchcard()
// ---
// Behind the code
// Without the _, .pianoroll() draws
// behind the whole editor instead of
// under one line.
//
// Try: .punchcard() or .spiral()
// instead.

setcpm(30)
$: n("0 2 4 <6 7> 4 2")
  .scale("C:minor")
  .s("triangle")
  .pianoroll()
